  <!-- In-Depth Clinical Guide: Root Canal Treatment in Hennur -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6 lg:px-24 bg-japandi-sand/25 border-y border-japandi-clay/30">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          Understanding Modern Root Canal Therapy (RCT) in Hennur
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Inside every tooth beneath the white enamel and hard dentin lies a soft vital tissue chamber called the dental pulp. The pulp contains nerves, blood vessels, and connective tissue essential during a tooth's growth. However, when deep bacterial decay, extensive cracks, repeated dental fillings, or physical trauma breach this chamber, bacteria multiply rapidly. This results in severe inflammation (pulpitis), intense throbbing pain, and eventually periapical bone abscesses.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Historically, teeth with infected pulp were extracted, leaving gaps that required costly bridges or implants. Root canal treatment is a biologically conservative therapy that eliminates the bacterial infection, thoroughly sterilizes the complex microscopic root canal anatomy, and seals the internal root with biocompatible materials—allowing you to keep your natural tooth for decades.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step-by-Step Procedure Guide -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          The 5-Stage Comfortable RCT Protocol at Aureva Dental Hennur
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Here is exactly what happens during your root canal appointment at our Horamavu Agara Road clinic:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 1: High-Definition RVG Imaging &amp; Buffered Numbing</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              We take high-resolution digital radiographs using our low-radiation RVG sensor to accurately map the curvature and number of your tooth's root canals. A topical numbing gel is gently applied to the gums, followed by a buffered computerized local anesthetic that renders the entire jaw numb within minutes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 2: Sterile Rubber Dam Isolation &amp; Pulp Access</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              We place a sterile dental dam sheet over the tooth. This isolates the tooth from oral saliva, prevents any bacterial contamination, and ensures none of the antiseptic rinsing liquids enter your mouth. A microscopic access opening is gently made through the crown to reach the infected pulp chamber.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 3: Electronic Apex Location &amp; Rotary NiTi Canal Shaping</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Using a digital electronic apex locator, we measure the exact microscopic length of each root canal with sub-millimeter precision. Motorized rotary nickel-titanium (NiTi) files then smoothly clean, debride, and contour the canals without manual file pressure, preserving the natural root walls.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 4: Ultrasonic Disinfection &amp; 3D Gutta-Percha Hermetic Seal</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Canals are flushed using warm antibacterial irrigants activated by ultrasonic vibration to dissolve deep microbial biofilm in microscopic side-canals. Once completely sterile and dried, the canals are obturated with thermoplastic gutta-percha and biocompatible resin sealer, creating an impermeable 3D seal.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 5: Core Rebuild &amp; High-Strength Zirconia Crown</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              A high-strength composite core buildup is bonded inside the tooth to restore structural integrity. We then custom-design a precision CAD/CAM Zirconia or ceramic crown to encase the tooth, ensuring it withstands normal biting pressure without cracking.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Transparent Root Canal Cost in Hennur Table Section -->
      <div id="pricing" class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-japandi-clay/30">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-japandi-moss">Transparent Pricing</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
            Root Canal Treatment &amp; Crown Cost in Hennur
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
            Fees depend on tooth position, canal complexity, and restorative material choice. A transparent written treatment plan is provided prior to commencing care.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-japandi-clay/40 bg-japandi-sand/30">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
            <thead class="bg-japandi-sand/80 text-japandi-charcoal font-medium border-b border-japandi-clay/40">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-4">Endodontic Procedure</th>
                <th class="p-4">Clinical Scope</th>
                <th class="p-4">Published Fee (INR)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-japandi-clay/20">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">New Patient Consultation + RVG X-Ray</td>
                <td class="p-4">Clinical examination &amp; digital radiograph</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹600</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Anterior Tooth Root Canal</td>
                <td class="p-4">Single canal endodontic therapy (front teeth)</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹4,000 – ₹6,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Premolar Root Canal</td>
                <td class="p-4">Intermediate 1–2 canal endodontic treatment</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹5,000 – ₹8,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Molar Root Canal</td>
                <td class="p-4">Multi-canal posterior endodontic treatment (3–4 canals)</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹6,000 – ₹10,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Re-Root Canal Treatment</td>
                <td class="p-4">Retreatment of previously failing root canals</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹8,000 onwards</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Dental Crown — Ceramic / PFM</td>
                <td class="p-4">PFM or all-ceramic restoration</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹5,000 – ₹10,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Dental Crown — Monolithic Zirconia</td>
                <td class="p-4">High-strength, metal-free CAD/CAM zirconia crown</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹10,000 – ₹18,000</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Clinical Comparison: Root Canal vs. Tooth Extraction -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Root Canal vs. Extraction: Why Saving Your Natural Tooth is Superior
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          When suffering from agonizing toothache, patients often ask if simply pulling the tooth is faster or cheaper. While tooth extraction may appear cheaper initially, the downstream anatomical and financial costs are substantially higher:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Consequences of Tooth Extraction</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Immediate bone loss: The jawbone where the tooth root was anchored shrinks in width within the first 12 months.</li>
              <li>Shifting of neighboring teeth: Adjacent teeth tilt into the empty socket gap, disrupting bite alignment and triggering TMJ discomfort.</li>
              <li>Opposing tooth supra-eruption: The tooth above or below the gap drifts downward or upward, loosening and becoming vulnerable to decay.</li>
              <li>Substantially higher future replacement costs: Replacing the missing gap requires a dental implant or 3-unit bridge costing 3x to 5x more.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Advantages of Root Canal Therapy</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Natural proprioception: You preserve natural periodontal ligament fibers that provide tactile chewing sensation and bite feedback.</li>
              <li>Permanent jawbone stability: The natural tooth root prevents localized alveolar bone resorption, maintaining natural facial contours.</li>
              <li>Full chewing efficiency: Once reinforced with a CAD/CAM zirconia crown, the tooth withstands full chewing forces.</li>
              <li>Biologically conservative: Only infected pulp tissue is removed; your original enamel, dentin, and root structure remain intact.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Post-Treatment Recovery and Home Care Timeline -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Post-RCT Care &amp; Recovery Timeline: What to Expect in 48 Hours
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Modern rotary root canal treatment causes minimal tissue trauma. Here is our recommended home care protocol following your procedure:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">First 2 to 4 Hours</span>
            <p>Wait until local numbness completely dissipates before eating to prevent cheek or tongue biting. Avoid hot beverages while numb.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
